{"step_index":1227,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T23:44:00Z","thinking":"**Constructing the Benchmark**\n\nI'm now building a payload-dependent benchmark, specifically for `ops/runtime/dynamic_payload_crdt_proof.zig`. The initial step involves utilizing dynamic pseudorandom payload data, potentially leveraging `std.crypto.random` or an LCG with a carefully selected seed to ensure adequate coverage and variability in test inputs. The aim is to create a robust and representative benchmark for this scenario.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// ops/runtime/dynamic_payload_crdt_proof.zig\n// Dynamic Payload-Dependent Blackbox Readback Benchmark for Sovra CRDT Graph\n// Eliminates algebraic loop reduction by deriving checksums from dynamic, non-predictable node memory contents.\n\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\nconst print = std.debug.print;\nconst crdt = @import(\"sovra_crdt_kernel.zig\");\n\nconst c = @cImport({\n    @cInclude(\"time.h\");\n});\n\nfn getNanos() u64 {\n    var ts: c.struct_timespec = undefined;\n    _ = c.clock_gettime(c.CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);\n    return @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_sec)) * 1_000_000_000 + @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_nsec));\n}\n\nfn volatileWrite(ptr: *volatile u64, val: u64) void {\n    ptr.* = val;\n}\n\n// Linear Congruential Generator for non-algebraic, dynamic payload data\nfn nextRandom(state: *u64) u64 {\n    state.* = state.* *% 6364136223846793005 +% 1442695040888963407;\n    return state.*;\n}\n\npub fn main() !void {\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n    print(\" DYNAMIC PAYLOAD-DEPENDENT CRDT BENCHMARK (M4 PHYSICAL SILICON)\\n\", .{});\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\\n\", .{});\n\n    var graph = crdt.SovraCrdtGraph.init();\n    var rng_seed: u64 = 0xDEADBEEFCAFE1001;\n\n    // 1. Warmup Iteration (10,000 insertions)\n    var w: u64 = 0;\n    while (w < 10000) : (w += 1) {\n        const payload_val = @as(u8, @intCast(nextRandom(&rng_seed) % 255));\n        _ = graph.insert_node(w + 1, .Episode, payload_val, 0);\n    }\n    graph.node_count = 0; // Reset arena\n    rng_seed = 0xFEEDBEEF12345678;\n\n    // 2. Volatile Sink setup\n    var volatile_checksum: u64 = 0;\n    const volatile_ptr: *volatile u64 = &volatile_checksum;\n\n    // 3. High-resolution Monotonic Nanosecond Timer\n    const t0 = getNanos();\n\n    var i: u64 = 0;\n    while (i < 100000) : (i += 1) {\n        // Generate unpredictable dynamic node payload\n        const dyn_payload = @as(u8, @intCast(nextRandom(&rng_seed) % 255));\n        const ok = graph.insert_node(\n            i + 1,\n            if (dyn_payload % 2 == 0) .Episode else .Semantic,\n            dyn_payload,\n            if (i > 0) i else 0,\n        );\n        if (ok) {\n            // Checksum depends strictly on actual written memory contents of node array in RAM\n            const written_node = graph.nodes[graph.node_count - 1];\n            const payload_hash = @as(u64, written_node.payload_val) *% 1099511628211 +% written_node.version_vector;\n            volatileWrite(volatile_ptr, volatile_ptr.* +% payload_hash);\n        }\n    }\n\n    const t1 = getNanos();\n    const total_ns = t1 - t0;\n    const total_us = total_ns / 1000;\n    const ns_per_op = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(total_ns)) / 100000.0;\n    const cycles_per_op = ns_per_op * 3.8; // M4 ~3.8 GHz clock frequency (1 cycle = ~0.263 ns)\n\n    print(\"[REAL HARDWARE MEASUREMENT RESULTS]\\n\", .{});\n    print(\"Total Nodes Inserted          : {}\\n\", .{graph.node_count});\n    print(\"Dynamic Checksum (Consumed)  : {} (Payload-Dependent Memory Hash)\\n\", .{volatile_checksum});\n    print(\"Total Time Elapsed (ns)       : {} ns\\n\", .{total_ns});\n    print(\"Total Time Elapsed (us)       : {} us ({d:.3} ms)\\n\", .{ total_us, @as(f64, @floatFromInt(total_us)) / 1000.0 });\n    print(\"Un-Elided Latency / Op        : {d:.2} ns / insertion\\n\", .{ns_per_op});\n    print(\"M4 CPU Cycles / Op (@3.8GHz)  : {d:.2} cycles / insertion\\n\\n\", .{cycles_per_op});\n\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n}\n","Description":"Creating dynamic payload-dependent CRDT benchmark in Zig","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/dynamic_payload_crdt_proof.zig","toolAction":"Writing dynamic_payload_crdt_proof.zig","toolSummary":"Writing dynamic_payload_crdt_proof.zig"}}]}
