{"step_index":1264,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T23:48:30Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Micro-Architecture**\n\nI've just completed Task-1260 and am now outlining a detailed engineering plan. The initial phase will concentrate on micro-architectural Store-to-Load Forwarding (STLF) and decoupled hardware experimentation. I'll begin with a detailed analysis of STLF stalls within the `dynamic_payload_crdt_` context. Further, I will look at hardware decoupling strategies.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// ops/runtime/decoupled_stlf_proof.zig\n// Decoupled STLF Hardware Benchmark for Apple Silicon M4\n// Separates Store Pass from Readback Pass to eliminate Store-to-Load Forwarding dependency bubbles.\n\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\nconst print = std.debug.print;\nconst crdt = @import(\"sovra_crdt_kernel.zig\");\n\nconst c = @cImport({\n    @cInclude(\"time.h\");\n});\n\nfn getNanos() u64 {\n    var ts: c.struct_timespec = undefined;\n    _ = c.clock_gettime(c.CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);\n    return @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_sec)) * 1_000_000_000 + @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_nsec));\n}\n\nfn volatileWrite(ptr: *volatile u64, val: u64) void {\n    ptr.* = val;\n}\n\nfn nextRandom(state: *u64) u64 {\n    state.* = state.* *% 6364136223846793005 +% 1442695040888963407;\n    return state.*;\n}\n\npub fn main() !void {\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n    print(\" DECOUPLED STLF STALL & PMU HARDWARE PROOF (M4 SILICON)\\n\", .{});\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\\n\", .{});\n\n    var graph = crdt.SovraCrdtGraph.init();\n    var rng_seed: u64 = 0x123456789ABCDEF0;\n\n    // Warmup\n    var w: u64 = 0;\n    while (w < 10000) : (w += 1) {\n        _ = graph.insert_node(w + 1, .Episode, @as(u8, @intCast(w % 255)), 0);\n    }\n    graph.node_count = 0;\n    rng_seed = 0x9876543210ABCDEF;\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // PASS 1: PURE RETIRED STORES PASS (No interleaved load readback)\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    const t_store0 = getNanos();\n\n    var i: u64 = 0;\n    while (i < 100000) : (i += 1) {\n        const dyn_payload = @as(u8, @intCast(nextRandom(&rng_seed) % 255));\n        _ = graph.insert_node(\n            i + 1,\n            if (dyn_payload % 2 == 0) .Episode else .Semantic,\n            dyn_payload,\n            if (i > 0) i else 0,\n        );\n    }\n\n    const t_store1 = getNanos();\n    const store_ns = t_store1 - t_store0;\n    const store_ns_per_op = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(store_ns)) / 100000.0;\n    const store_cycles_per_op = store_ns_per_op * 3.8;\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // PASS 2: PURE RETIRED READBACK PASS (Non-interleaved volatile checksum)\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    var volatile_checksum: u64 = 0;\n    const volatile_ptr: *volatile u64 = &volatile_checksum;\n\n    const t_read0 = getNanos();\n\n    var j: usize = 0;\n    while (j < graph.node_count) : (j += 1) {\n        const node = graph.nodes[j];\n        const payload_hash = @as(u64, node.confidence_byte) *% 1099511628211 \n                            +% @as(u64, @intCast(node.id & 0xFFFFFFFF)) \n                            +% node.version_vector;\n        volatileWrite(volatile_ptr, volatile_ptr.* +% payload_hash);\n    }\n\n    const t_read1 = getNanos();\n    const read_ns = t_read1 - t_read0;\n    const read_ns_per_op = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(read_ns)) / 100000.0;\n    const read_cycles_per_op = read_ns_per_op * 3.8;\n\n    const combined_ns = store_ns + read_ns;\n\n    print(\"--- [DECOUPLED HARDWARE EXECUTION BREAKDOWN] ---\\n\", .{});\n    print(\"1. PURE STORE PASS (100,000 Inserts) : {} ns ({d:.3} ms)\\n\", .{ store_ns, @as(f64, @floatFromInt(store_ns)) / 1000000.0 });\n    print(\"   -> Store Latency per Op            : {d:.2} ns / op\\n\", .{store_ns_per_op});\n    print(\"   -> M4 Store CPU Cycles / Op        : {d:.2} cycles / op\\n\\n\", .{store_cycles_per_op});\n\n    print(\"2. PURE READBACK PASS (100,000 Reads): {} ns ({d:.3} ms)\\n\", .{ read_ns, @as(f64, @floatFromInt(read_ns)) / 1000000.0 });\n    print(\"   -> Read Latency per Op             : {d:.2} ns / op\\n\", .{read_ns_per_op});\n    print(\"   -> M4 Read CPU Cycles / Op         : {d:.2} cycles / op\\n\\n\", .{read_cycles_per_op});\n\n    print(\"3. COMBINED DECOUPLED LATENCY        : {} ns ({d:.3} ms)\\n\", .{ combined_ns, @as(f64, @floatFromInt(combined_ns)) / 1000000.0 });\n    print(\"   -> Volatile Checksum (Consumed)    : {} (Blackbox Readback Proof)\\n\\n\", .{volatile_checksum});\n\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n}\n","Description":"Creating decoupled STLF benchmark in Zig to isolate stores and loads","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/decoupled_stlf_proof.zig","toolAction":"Writing decoupled_stlf_proof.zig","toolSummary":"Writing decoupled_stlf_proof.zig"}}]}
